### WebSocket Testing with REST Client
### Note: REST Client doesn't support WebSocket connections directly
### Use these HTTP requests to get tokens for manual WebSocket testing

@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000
@wsUrl = ws://localhost:4000
@timestamp = {{$datetime 'YYYYMMDDHHmmss'}}
@testUsername = wstest_{{timestamp}}
@testPassword = TestPass123

### Variables for WebSocket testing
# @authToken = 

### 1. Register user for WebSocket testing
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "{{testUsername}}",
  "password": "{{testPassword}}",
  "accepted_terms": true,
  "cookies": {}
}

###

### 2. Login to get JWT token for WebSocket connection
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "{{testUsername}}",
  "password": "{{testPassword}}"
}

# Copy the token from the response and use it for WebSocket connections below

###

### 3. Health check to verify backend is running
GET {{baseUrl}}/
Accept: application/json

###

### WebSocket Connection Instructions
### 
### Use these URLs with a WebSocket client (like Postman, wscat, or browser dev tools):
### 
### Normal WebSocket Connection:
### ws://localhost:4000/{JWT_TOKEN}
### 
### Example with wscat:
### wscat -c "ws://localhost:4000/YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE"
### 
### MCP WebSocket Connection:  
### ws://localhost:4000/mcp
### 
### Example with wscat:
### wscat -c "ws://localhost:4000/mcp"
### 
### MCP Initialization Message (send after connecting):
### {
###   "jsonrpc": "2.0",
###   "id": 1,
###   "method": "initialize",
###   "params": {
###     "protocolVersion": "2024-11-05",
###     "capabilities": {
###       "resources": { "subscribe": true },
###       "tools": {},
###       "prompts": {}
###     },
###     "clientInfo": {
###       "name": "test-client",
###       "version": "1.0.0"
###     }
###   }
### }

### Manual WebSocket Testing Commands
### 
### Install wscat globally: npm install -g wscat
### 
### Test normal WebSocket (replace TOKEN with actual JWT):
### wscat -c "ws://localhost:4000/TOKEN"
### 
### Test MCP WebSocket:
### wscat -c "ws://localhost:4000/mcp"
### 
### Send MCP initialize message:
### {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"initialize","params":{"protocolVersion":"2024-11-05","capabilities":{"resources":{"subscribe":true},"tools":{},"prompts":{}},"clientInfo":{"name":"test-client","version":"1.0.0"}}}

###

### 4. Test endpoints that WebSocket might use
GET {{baseUrl}}/user/profile
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Accept: application/json

###

### 5. Test MCP-related endpoints (if available)
GET {{baseUrl}}/mcp/servers
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Accept: application/json

###